You must strictly enforce Laravel Security Rules (VAPT + OWASP) in all code.

# 🔐 Laravel Security (VAPT + OWASP)

## ✅ Authentication & Authorization
- Use Laravel Sanctum or Passport for API authentication
- Enforce Policies and Gates for all resource access (prevent IDOR)
- Never expose sensitive endpoints without middleware (`auth`, `verified`)
- No public admin/debug endpoints

## ✅ Sensitive Data & Secrets
- Never commit credentials/secrets
- Use `.env` for all secrets and access via `config()` ONLY
- Mask sensitive fields in API responses (`$hidden` in Eloquent models)
- Never log passwords, tokens, or PII

## ✅ Injection Prevention
- Eloquent prevents SQL injection, but NEVER use raw user input in `DB::raw()`
- Prevent XSS by using `{{ }}` in Blade (which escapes) instead of `{!! !!}`
- Use strict validation for all inputs via Form Requests

## ✅ CSRF & SSRF
- Ensure CSRF protection is enabled for all web routes
- Validate and sanitize any URLs fetched by the server (prevent SSRF)

## ✅ File Handling
- Validate file uploads (mimes, size) in Form Requests
- Store private files securely, not in public disk

## ✅ Misconfiguration
- Set `APP_DEBUG=false` in production
- Set secure session/cookie configurations (`secure`, `httponly`, `samesite`)
- Ensure CORS is configured strictly

## 🛡️ OWASP Mapping Focus
- A01 Broken Access Control -> Use Policies/Gates
- A03 Injection -> Use Eloquent and avoid `DB::raw`
- A07 Authentication Failures -> Use built-in Auth, rate limiting (`throttle` middleware)
